62                B_VAR:    (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Variable in M_DS with baseline measurements
63                REF_TRTN: (Leave blank to omit p-value from summary table.) Numeric value of TN_VAR for reference (comparator)
63       ! treatment
64                B_VISN: Visit number that represents Baseline in AVISITN (e.g., 0)
65                E_VISN: Visit number that represents endpoint in AVISITN for chg-from-baseline comparison (e.g., 99)
66                        OPTIONAL: Include additional visits BETWEEN baseline and endpoint.
67                                  List space-delimited, INCREASING visit numbers in E_VISN.
68                                  The LAST (greatest) visit number in E_VISN is the endpoint visit.
69                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
70                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates that record is selected for analysis.
71                REF_LINES:
72                      Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
73                      <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
74                      NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
75                      UNIFORM - Preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if they are uniform for all
75       ! measurements
76                      NARROW  - Default. Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
77                      ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
78                      numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
